      {
        "id": "p22-q89a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}=\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n}=\\frac{n-(n-1)}{n(n-1)}=\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n}&=\\frac{n-(n-1)}{n(n-1)}\\\\\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n}&=\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q89b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p22-q89b-prompt-hence",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hence, show that",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p22-q89b-prompt-sum",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{1}{\\ln(2)\\ln(4)}+\\frac{1}{\\ln(4)\\ln(8)}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{\\ln(2^{n-1})\\ln(2^n)}",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p22-q89b-prompt-result",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "is equal to ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)(\\log_2 e)^2",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p22-q89b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)(\\log_2 e)^2",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p22-q89b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\ln(2^k)=k\\ln2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and part (a) to cancel consecutive terms, then use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\log_2 e=\\frac{1}{\\ln2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $k=2,3,\\ldots,n$, the power law gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(2^{k-1})\\ln(2^k)&=(k-1)\\ln2\\times k\\ln2\\\\\\ln(2^{k-1})\\ln(2^k)&=k(k-1)(\\ln2)^2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nLet $S$ denote the given sum. Using part (a),\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac{1}{(\\ln2)^2}\\left(\\frac{1}{1\\cdot2}+\\frac{1}{2\\cdot3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{(n-1)n}\\right)\\\\S&=\\frac{1}{(\\ln2)^2}\\left[\\left(1-\\frac12\\right)+\\left(\\frac12-\\frac13\\right)+\\cdots+\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac1n\\right)\\right]\\\\S&=\\frac{1}{(\\ln2)^2}\\left(1-\\frac1n\\right).\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy change of base,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2 e&=\\frac{\\ln e}{\\ln2}\\\\\\log_2 e&=\\frac{1}{\\ln2}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$S=\\left(1-\\frac1n\\right)(\\log_2 e)^2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
